<title>USA: Alco's Unisource acquires 41 businesses.</title>
<headline>Alco's Unisource acquires 41 businesses.</headline>
<dateline>VALLEY FORGE, Pa. 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Alco Standard Corp's Unisource Worldwide Inc said on Tuesday that it completed 41 acquisitions in the fiscal year ended September 1996 with annualized revenues totaling more than $850 million.</p>
<p>Unisource said it plans to acquire businesses to generate at least $500 million in annualized revenues for each of the next three fiscal years.</p>
<p>Unisource is the largest marketer and distributor of paper and supply systems in North America and will begin operating as a separate publicly traded company in 1997, Unisource said.</p>
<p>At Alco Standard, Unisource generated 71 percent of the revenues of $9.89 billion and 47 percent of the profits of $202.7 million.</p>
</text>
